OS-RELEASE(5)

# NAME

os-release - operating system release information file

# SYNOPSIS

*/etc/os-release*
; */usr/lib/os-release*

# DESCRIPTION

The _/etc/os-release_
; and _/usr/lib/os-release_ files
provide basic release information about the operating system.
Format is KEY="Value".
Values may be quoted if they contain spaces or special characters.
Entries can appear in any order.
All entries are optional; new ones may be added in future.

The common keys are as follows:

*NAME*
	Operating system name (no version).

*PRETTY_NAME*
	Operating system name with version.

*ID*
	Short identifier string.
	For Zeppe-Lin, use "zeppe-lin".

*CPE_NAME*
	Common Platform Enumeration (CPE) name, as defined by
	https://scap.nist.gov/specifications/cpe/.

*VERSION*
	Version string, human-readable.

*VERSION_ID*
	Version string suitable for scripts
	(lowercase letters, digits, ".", "-", "\_").

*VARIANT*
	Human-readable release type.

*VARIANT_ID*
	Release type identifier suitable for scripts
	(lowercase letters, digits, ".", "-", "\_").

*BUILD_ID*
	Detailed build identifier.

*HOME_URL*, *SUPPORT_URL*
	URLs for information or support.

# EXAMPLES

The following example shows a _/etc/os-release_ for Zeppe-Lin Linux
1.2.1, though actual contents may vary.

```
NAME="Zeppe-Lin"
VERSION="1.2.1 (Ghosts in the Rig)"
ID="zeppe-lin"
VERSION_ID="1.2.1"
PRETTY_NAME="Zeppe-Lin 1.2.1 (Ghosts in the Rig)"
HOME_URL="https://zeppe-lin.org/"
SUPPORT_URL="mailto:zeppe-lin@freelists.org"
BUG_REPORT_URL="mailto:zeppe-lin-dev@freelists.org"
```

# FILES

_/etc/os-release_
	Operating system release information.

# SEE ALSO

*uname*(1)

https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/os-release.html

# HISTORY

The _/etc/os-release_  file was added in Zeppe-Lin 2.0 to provide
standard operating system identification data for userland tools and
scripts.

